From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: husky-port CI <ci@husky-port.local>
Date: Fri, 7 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb: defer probe when s2mpu device is not
 registered yet

exynos_usbdrd_phy_probe() looks up the s2mpu platform device via the
"s2mpus" phandle.  When the phy probes before the pkvm-s2mpu driver has
registered its platform device, of_find_device_by_node() returns NULL
and phy_drd->s2mpu stays NULL forever: every exynos_usbdrd_s2mpu_manual_control()
call then silently returns without configuring the S2MPU, and the first
USB gadget DMA access faults in the HSI0 SysMMU (PTW access permission
fault).  Stock Android avoids the race with a fixed module load order;
module loading via uevents hits it ~50% of boots.

Return -EPROBE_DEFER when the phandle exists but the device has not been
registered yet, so the driver core re-probes after the s2mpu device
appears.  Restores the stock manual_control/notify code path (no
workaround needed).

---
--- a/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c
+++ b/soc/gs/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb.c
@@ -2057,7 +2057,10 @@ static int exynos_usbdrd_phy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	s2mpu_np = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "s2mpus", 0);
 	if (s2mpu_np) {
 		s2mpu_pdev = of_find_device_by_node(s2mpu_np);
 		of_node_put(s2mpu_np);
+		/* The S2MPU platform device may not be registered yet. */
+		if (!s2mpu_pdev)
+			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
 	}
 
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_EXYNOS_PD_HSI0)
